net.Listen{,TCP,UDP,Unix,Packet} and {syscall,unix}.{Socket,Bind,Listen} were
declared net_recv, which AUTO_SOURCE_LABEL_MAP collapses to untrusted_input, so
each minted untrusted input at a call that returns a file descriptor and
nothing else. They are ADR-0049 ruling 1 deferred crossings and move to
net_listen -- the first catalogue rows to use the boundary WI-nosah built.

MEASURED on an idiomatic Go accept loop (net.Listen -> ln.Accept -> conn.Read):
BEFORE 8 net_recv chains, every one a setup or launch call and ZERO true
receives. AFTER 7 net_listen + 1 net_recv. Every crossing still represented;
nothing dropped. That is ADR-0049 ruling 3 met on a run, not argued from rows.

RETAG, NOT REMOVAL, which is what unblocked an item blocked by its own
reasoning. INV-kanuk had recorded that removal was NOT licensed: go's real
receive surface is unreachable on idiomatic code, so deleting the rows would
take go's network-input surface to nothing rather than relocating it -- the
WI-lunav failure at eight rows. A retag has no such problem. The call is still
classified, so it still counts as examined under INV-buzab, and the net_listen
shadow QUALIFIES a clean net_recv verdict instead of granting one. Asserted end
to end: the same edge and claim that returned a bare confirmed before now
return confirmed_with_caveats naming the site.

THE LAUNCH ROWS DELIBERATELY DID NOT MOVE, IN ANY LANGUAGE. net/http's
ListenAndServe, gin's Run, echo's Start, fiber's Listen and grpc's Serve are
equally deferred crossings, and they are pinned together across nine languages
by TestServerLaunchStaysAReceive until ADR-0049 open-work step 3 (adjudicated
findings per shape) clears. Steps 1, 2 and 4 are done -- WI-hazop, WI-vapud /
measurement 0009, and the INV-buzab check. Step 3 is not. I first moved all 21
rows; the pin went red on net/http.Serve and the scope was narrowed to the
SETUP rows this item's statement actually names. The pin firing is why this is
11 rows and not 21.

The F2 gate's language-wide go exemption is replaced by a ROW-level one.
fiber's App.Listen survives the widened gate as a FALSE POSITIVE OF THE
PREDICATE -- it blocks and serves, so it is launch rather than setup, and it is
caught only because the predicate matches lowercase NAMES while the family is
cut by MECHANISM. F2_EXEMPT_ROWS excuses that single (module, name) pair, a
companion test fails if the row is ever retagged or removed, and the repro
assertion pins the EXACT remaining offender rather than asserting empty --
an empty assertion would have forced either a wrong retag or a language-wide
skip, and both hide a row.

